From 204d1b534d01fb9d6a7ff2b3f62e06780437290d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Metacraft Labs <info@metacraft-labs.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:53:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Don't strand queued jobs when the job cache goes stale

consumeQueuedJobs() trusts the pool manager's in-memory job cache, which
is fed only by watcher notifications. A pass that cannot place a job
locks it, fails, and unlocks it within about a millisecond. If the
unlock notification is lost, or arrives before the lock's, the cache
says "locked by us" while the store says unlocked.

The 10 minute retry cannot repair that. UnlockJob() on an already
unlocked row is a silent no-op that sends no notification, and the
check that follows reads the same stale cached LockedBy and skips the
job. It is skipped on every pass, even after capacity frees up, until
the controller restarts.

Write the manager's own lock and unlock through to the cache by
re-reading the row from the store (refreshCachedJob). Once the 10
minute path has unlocked the row, treat the local copy as unlocked and
retry it in the same pass. If LockJob() or UnlockJob() reports that a
cached job is gone from the store, drop it from the cache instead of
retrying it forever or aborting the rest of the pass.

Signed-off-by: Metacraft Labs <info@metacraft-labs.com>
---
 runner/pool/pool.go      |  38 ++++++++++++++
 runner/pool/pool_test.go | 105 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 runner/pool/util.go      |  48 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 191 insertions(+)

